Use case: stylized-concept.
Asset type: production sprite sheet for a GBA-style side-view 2D fighting game.
Create a SINGLE sprite sheet containing EIGHT separate full-body sprites of the SAME Pokémon character. Output a wide 2:1 canvas, preferably 1536 x 768. Arrange the eight sprites in an EXACT REGULAR GRID of FOUR equal-width columns and TWO equal-height rows, read left to right. There are no visible grid lines. Every cell has one character with generous completely transparent margin; no character or effects may cross a cell boundary.
The poses in exact reading order:
row 1 column 1: idle guard pose;
row 1 column 2: alternate idle guard, slightly shifted head and limbs;
row 1 column 3: running forward first stride;
row 1 column 4: running forward opposite stride;
row 2 column 1: attack anticipation, leaning back;
row 2 column 2: attack release, extended toward the right, small self-contained species-specific elemental effect;
row 2 column 3: hurt recoil, still on feet;
row 2 column 4: knocked out lying down, eyes closed.
ALL sprites FACE RIGHT in side or three-quarter-side view, consistent visible right-facing eye and mouth direction. Same character proportions, same scale and palette across all cells. Each standing character has feet on a consistent baseline at 85% of its cell height; all anatomy including ears and tails stays inside its own cell with at least 12% margin.
Style: authentic early-2000s handheld pixel art, carefully drawn low-resolution game sprites, strong single-pixel dark outlines, crisp hard-edged square pixels, small 16-color character palette, 3 tones per color, no anti-aliasing, NO smooth painting or gradients, no 3D or vector look. The character should look like a compact 48-to-56-pixel-tall sprite enlarged using nearest-neighbor pixels, readable when reduced to a 64x64 frame.
Background: REAL transparent alpha. No opaque background, no checkerboard drawn into the pixels, no floor plane, no ground shadows, no labels, no UI, no borders, no watermark, no additional characters. Preserve recognizable canonical Pokémon identity.
Subject: Pikachu, the unevolved yellow electric mouse Pokémon: long upright black-tipped ears, red cheek circles, brown back stripes, lightning-bolt tail. Attack effect: short golden electric sparks to the right. Do not use Pichu, Raichu, clothes, or props.

